# Vulnerable Internal Document Management System

This repository contains a deliberately vulnerable internal document management system built to demonstrate real-world web application security failures, including Insecure Direct Object References (IDOR), broken access control, and authorization logic flaws.

The project is intended for educational and portfolio purposes and reflects how production systems often fail due to backend trust assumptions and inconsistent authorization enforcement, rather than missing authentication mechanisms.

## Repository Structure

- `vulnerable/` – Intentionally insecure implementation of the application, including setup instructions and threat model context.
- `reports/` – Detailed vulnerability reports documenting root cause, exploitation, impact, and recommended fixes.
- `fixes/` – Hardened version of the application with systematic and well-documented security improvements.

## Requirements

- Python 3.11
- FastAPI
- Uvicorn
- SQLAlchemy
- PostgreSQL (`psycopg2-binary`)
- Passlib (`bcrypt` 3.2.2)
- python-multipart

## Disclaimer

This application is insecure by design and must only be run in a local, controlled environment for educational purposes.
